## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to design governance-compliant, explainable ML systems for regulated fintech environments at scale.

## Key Concepts

- Policy engine with semantic versioning and rule inheritance
- Feature masking for privacy and regulatory compliance
- Explainability through SHAP values for auditability
- Distributed tracing with OpenTelemetry across the pipeline
- Automated drift detection and model monitoring
- Immutable audit trails with cryptographic verification
- Instant rollback mechanisms for policy changes

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode for policy-driven scoring workflow
function computeCCAScore(user, features, policyVersion) {
  const policy = getPolicyVersion(policyVersion);
  const allowedFeatures = policy.filterAllowed(features);
  const maskedFeatures = policy.maskSensitive(allowedFeatures, user);
  const explanation = computeSHAP(maskedFeatures, model);
  const auditTrail = createImmutableLog({user, policyVersion, timestamp});

  return {
    score: model.predict(maskedFeatures),
    explanation: explanation,
    policyVersion: policyVersion,
    auditId: auditTrail.id
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates offline-first architecture design, conflict resolution strategies, and API robustness for clients with unreliable connectivity.

## Key Concepts
- Client-side caching with immediate response
- Version-based conflict resolution using sync tokens
- Idempotent operations for safe retries
- Batch synchronization for network efficiency
- Comprehensive testing under simulated outage conditions

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for offline sync workflow
const cache = new UserScoreCache();
const syncQueue = new OfflineQueue();

function computeCCAScore(userId, data) {
  const score = calculateScore(data);
  const token = cache.update(userId, score);
  syncQueue.enqueue({userId, score, token, timestamp: Date.now()});
  return score;
}

function syncToServer() {
  if (navigator.onLine) {
    const batch = syncQueue.getBatch();
    return fetch('/cca_score/sync', {
      method: 'POST',
      body: JSON.stringify(batch)
    }).then(response => {
      if (response.ok) syncQueue.confirmBatch();
    });
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle concurrent client modifications?
- What fallback strategies would you implement for extended outages?
- How would you optimize sync payload size for low-bandwidth connections?
